counterfactuals.output:
A computer-implemented method for automated portioning of a workpiece, the method comprising:

receiving, by a control system associated with a portioning apparatus, workpiece data representative of at least one physical characteristic of a workpiece to be cut;

storing, in a memory accessible by the control system, a plurality of reference coordinate sets, each reference coordinate set defining a desired geometric configuration of a corresponding portion to be produced from the workpiece;

providing an operator interface configured to permit editing of at least one reference coordinate of at least one of the plurality of reference coordinate sets, thereby modifying a desired shape of the corresponding portion without requiring direct manual specification of all cutting parameters;

generating, by the control system, a virtual representation of the workpiece and of one or more desired portions based at least in part on the workpiece data and the edited reference coordinate sets;

executing, prior to physical cutting of the workpiece, one or more simulation routines using the virtual representation to evaluate prospective cutting operations for producing the one or more desired portions;

determining, from the one or more simulation routines, at least one indirect physical specification associated with production of the one or more desired portions, the at least one indirect physical specification comprising a physical cutting parameter derived from the reference coordinate sets and the workpiece data rather than being directly specified by an operator;

selecting or adjusting a cutting plan based on the determined indirect physical specification; and

controlling, after completion of the simulation routines, at least one cutting device to cut the workpiece in accordance with the selected or adjusted cutting plan so as to produce portions corresponding to the desired geometric configurations defined by the edited reference coordinate sets.
